                <pb facs="0619" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/983: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sterling</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-06T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 6, 1922—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>63. Your no. 51, dated July 5, 5 p.m. I had an interview with President Leguía
                    this morning at the end of which he expressed <pb facs="0620" n="500"
                        xml:id="pg500"/> himself as being in favor of accepting the suggestion as it
                    is. He is consulting the Cabinet.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
